        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data. It performs static analysis only here: **no code is run**. We examined 1 R code file.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1L, File = \"reads_dta.R\", \"Runs after\" = \"—\", \n    Basis = \"none\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "**1 data path in the code does not work in the repository as deposited.** We would point it to where the file is, so the code could run: `../data/Data.DTA` to `data.dta` (in reads_dta.R). The code should be changed, because as written it does not find the file.",
          "**1 file name in the code is not the same as in the deposit**, in case, spaces or punctuation, and exactly one file in the deposit fits. To run the code we would correct this in a copy of the script so that it finds the file. The script itself should be changed, because as written it does not find the file on every system.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"reads_dta.R\", \"Name in the code\" = \"Data.DTA\", \n    \"Name in the deposit\" = \"data.dta\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L\n), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Missing inputs",
          "Every data file the code reads is either produced by an earlier script or present in the repository.",
          "*Executing the code is a separate, opt-in phase (run with `execute = TRUE`). This report describes what a run would involve; it did not run anything.*",
          "#### Stata data",
          "The Stata data file (`.dta`) is read by the deposit's own code, so the analysis is in that code, not in a Stata do-file."
